# Contract 5, app half. Copy to app/.env.local (git-ignored) and fill in what you need.
# Every key is optional: with none of them set the app talks to a local network and the
# built-in test wallets pay their own fees, which is the zero-secrets default.

# --- network ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# With VITE_API set, reads go through the backend's read-only proxy ($VITE_API/api/rpc): leave
# VITE_RPC unset and no RPC key is ever in the bundle. Without VITE_API it defaults to
# http://<this host>:8899 (Surfpool). Set VITE_RPC only to point at a local validator (and
# VITE_LOCAL=1 if the proxied backend itself runs against a local chain). Never put a paid RPC key
# here for a deployed build: it would be public. 429s are retried with backoff (app/src/lib/rpc.ts).
# VITE_RPC=http://localhost:8899
#
# Which cluster to name in a wallet signing request, so an extension simulates the transaction
# against the right chain instead of its own default (docs/wallet-simulation.md). Only needed when
# the app cannot work it out: with VITE_API set, VITE_RPC is the backend's proxy and its URL says
# nothing about what is behind it, so an unset value means devnet (localnet with VITE_LOCAL=1).
# Set it for anything else. devnet | mainnet | testnet | localnet.
# VITE_CLUSTER=devnet

# --- sponsored fees (contract 2) -------------------------------------------------------------
# Set VITE_API and every flow is routed through POST /api/sponsor, so the user needs no SOL.
# Leave it unset and the connected wallet pays its own fees (local test mode).
VITE_API=http://localhost:8787
# The fee payer's address is part of what the user signs, so the app has to know it up front.
# Set it here, or leave it blank and the app asks GET /api/sponsor for it.
VITE_FEE_PAYER=

# --- confidential balances -------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Token-2022 confidential mint rent is settled in (scripts/make-rusdc.ts creates it).
# Until it exists, private operations report that it is not configured.
VITE_RUSDC_MINT=

# --- embedded wallet: sign up with an email (workstream B) -----------------------------------
# Which provider backs "Continue with email" on the sign-up page. With BOTH of these unset the
# option is not offered and the app behaves exactly as it did before: extension wallets, plus the
# built-in test wallet on a local network.
#   mock   an email-derived keypair this page holds. Needs no secrets and no provider account, so
#          it is what the demo runs on. Labelled "demo wallet" in the UI, because the key is
#          derivable from the address — see the header of app/src/auth/mock.ts.
#   privy  a real hosted embedded wallet. Needs the app id below AND the SDK binding described at
#          the top of app/src/auth/privy.ts (the SDK is deliberately not a dependency yet).
VITE_EMBEDDED_WALLET=mock
# A Privy app id on its own selects privy, so VITE_EMBEDDED_WALLET only has to be set to override.
VITE_EMBEDDED_WALLET_APP_ID=

# Sign-up also needs VITE_API above: the wallet is exchanged for the backend session that
# POST /api/sponsor requires, which is what lets a wallet holding 0 SOL transact at all.

# --- operator verdict console (D2) -----------------------------------------------------------
# Serves the appraiser's verdict screen at #/appraiser. OFF unless this is exactly "1", and the
# flag is inlined at build time, so an unset build does not contain the screen at all (not just a
# dead route). Set it for the demo build only.
#
# The page holds no key: the appraiser's key is the BACKEND's (APPRAISER_KEYPAIRS) behind its own
# VERDICT_CONSOLE_TOKEN, which the operator pastes and which is never stored. See
# docs/contracts/dispute-mediation.md §10 and docs/env-checklist.md.
# VITE_APPRAISER_CONSOLE=1

# --- developer check only --------------------------------------------------------------------
# A throwaway devnet keypair (64-byte JSON array) that funds app/confidential-check.html.
# NEVER a real key: anything in a VITE_ variable is compiled into the page.
VITE_CT_PAYER=
